      <p>We collect the following types of information:</p>
      <ul>
        <li><strong>Account information:</strong> name, email address, and password when you register.</li>
        <li><strong>Health &amp; body data:</strong> height, weight, age, pain areas, fitness goals, and activity level you provide during onboarding and in settings.</li>
        <li><strong>Usage data:</strong> workouts completed, exercise history, routines created, and progress metrics.</li>
        <li><strong>Device information:</strong> browser type, operating system, and session data for security and functionality purposes.</li>
      </ul>
    </div>

    <!-- Section 2 -->
    <div class="pp-section">
      <h5 class="fw-semibold pp-heading">2. How We Use Your Information</h5>
      <p>Your information is used to:</p>
      <ul>
        <li>Provide and personalise your physiotherapy experience.</li>
        <li>Track your workout history, progress, and achievements.</li>
        <li>Send in-app notifications and reminders relevant to your goals.</li>
        <li>Improve the application based on usage patterns.</li>
        <li>Maintain account security and prevent unauthorised access.</li>
      </ul>
    </div>

    <!-- Section 3 -->
    <div class="pp-section">
      <h5 class="fw-semibold pp-heading">3. Data Sharing &amp; Third Parties</h5>
      <p>We do <strong>not</strong> sell, trade, or rent your personal information to third parties. We may share data only in the following limited cases:</p>
      <ul>
        <li><strong>Service providers:</strong> trusted partners who help us operate the app (e.g. hosting, database services), bound by confidentiality agreements.</li>
        <li><strong>Legal obligations:</strong> if required by law, court order, or to protect the rights and safety of our users.</li>
      </ul>
    </div>

    <!-- Section 4 -->
    <div class="pp-section">
      <h5 class="fw-semibold pp-heading">4. Cookies &amp; Session Data</h5>
      <p>
        PhysioApp uses session cookies to keep you logged in and maintain application state. These cookies are essential for the app to function and are not used for advertising or tracking across other websites. You can disable cookies in your browser settings, but this may affect app functionality.
      </p>
    </div>

    <!-- Section 5 -->
    <div class="pp-section">
      <h5 class="fw-semibold pp-heading">5. Data Security</h5>
      <p>
        We take reasonable technical and organisational measures to protect your data, including password hashing (bcrypt), session-based authentication, and optional two-factor authentication (2FA). However, no method of transmission over the internet is 100% secure, and we cannot guarantee absolute security.
      </p>
    </div>

    <!-- Section 6 -->
    <div class="pp-section">
      <h5 class="fw-semibold pp-heading">6. Your Rights</h5>
      <p>You have the right to:</p>
      <ul>
        <li>Access the personal data we hold about you.</li>
        <li>Correct inaccurate or incomplete information via your profile settings.</li>
        <li>Delete your account and associated data at any time from the settings page.</li>
        <li>Withdraw consent for any optional data processing.</li>
      </ul>
    </div>

    <!-- Section 7 -->
    <div class="pp-section">
      <h5 class="fw-semibold pp-heading">7. Data Retention</h5>
      <p>
        We retain your data for as long as your account is active. When you delete your account, your personal data and health information are permanently removed from our systems within 30 days.
      </p>
